  "summary": "A marketplace where hosts set their own prices. Each figure is a floor - the median of the five cheapest listings that Clore itself marks verified (\"rating above 4 with reviews\"), rentable and payable in dollars - withheld when too few are listed. Clore lists a price per day; the figure here is that price with the renter fee Clore charges, divided by 24, which is what its own table shows per hour. Machines with several GPUs and its spot market are not read.",
  "notes": "marketplace, keyless feed; trimmed floor of the 5 cheapest verified single-GPU on-demand listings, withheld when the window cannot carry a floor (fewer than 3 listings, or a median over 3x the cheapest ask); the feed prices per day and the renter fee is read from /marketplace/renter_fees each run, so the figure is price * 1.05 / 24; spot bids and multi-GPU machines not read",
